KLCS Linux compatibility payload root.

Local test ISOs can stage Linux tools here with:

  tools/stage_klcs_apps.sh

The staged binaries are intentionally local payloads for KLCS testing. KLCS can
now launch staged dynamic Linux ELF64 programs through the bundled ld-linux
bridge. This is not a complete Linux ABI, but basic glibc loader startup works.

Inside K64, these forms are accepted for staged tools:

  klcs run klcs-hello
  klcs run tcc -v
  klcs run nano --version
  klcs run git --version
  klcs run sl

klcs-hello is a static Linux x86_64 ELF built with K64 and should actually run
through the Linux syscall gate. sl is the real Debian amd64 sl binary staged
from the Debian package archive. Dynamically linked tools depend on staged
libraries and data files under /compat/linux/lib64, /compat/linux/usr/lib* and
/compat/linux/usr/share.
